From a26f505e7094de01d6ec422b5cdef721c0410c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:11:06 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] kcm_nightlight: state line first, mode as three
 options, schedule and preview built after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). kwinrc keys (Active, Mode, DayTemperature, NightTemperature), the org.kde.KWin.NightLight
D-Bus calls (preview, stopPreview, activate/deactivate*), KCMLauncher use and the colour-ramp code are unchanged.
NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- New first line (state): "Night Light is off." / "is always on." / "is on until 07:00." / "turns on at 19:30." (bold, centred;
  night is when the next transition is the morning one; computed from DayNightTimings). The temporary on/off
  InlineMessage keeps its place under it, then the day/night timeline preview.
- The "Switching times:" combo box (Always off / Always on / Sunrise and sunset) is now the Form option group
  "Night Light:" with radio buttons Off / Always on / At sunset, until sunrise (three short exclusive options, section 3).
  Same writes as before (Mode first, then Active). The old sentence "The blue light filter makes the colors on the screen
  warmer." is the small help under the options instead of a centred paragraph at the top.
- The icon-only "Configure…" button (tooltip only) is now the labelled link "Day-Night Cycle…" (openSystemSettings
  "kcm_nighttime"), still disabled unless the mode is the sunrise/sunset one (ia/duplicates.md: Night Light vs Day-Night).
- Section "Temperature" (noun) holds the two sliders ("Day light temperature:", "Night light temperature:"), same keys.
  Page is KCM.SimpleKCM + Kirigami.FormLayout (was Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry).
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_nightlight.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 17 rows ok, 0 lost.
- HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-057; page-design sections 2, 3, 7.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured):
- DayNightView (25 axis labels, three icon delegates, a 50-line colour table) and a DayNightTimings (which makes a
  KDarkLightScheduleProvider) were created with the page, inside the form. Now both sit in Loaders that become active one
  event-loop turn after the first frame (the preview Loader is asynchronous); the page height of the preview is reserved.
- DayNightView's "now" marker Timer had interval 60 (ms), repeating forever: a wake-up every 60 ms for a marker that moves
  one pixel every few minutes. Now 60000 ms (triggeredOnStart keeps the first position).
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: Loader.item of a non-Item sourceComponent (DayNightTimings) used as a QObject; DayNightView
properties set from a Component under `pragma ComponentBehavior: Bound`; KDarkLightScheduleProvider's own blocking cost (its
source is outside plasma-workspace, not read).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
